{"v":1,"ts":"5Z4J525MWB819ZK","kind":"task.created","project":"endless","entity":{"type":"task","id":"2032"},"actor":{"kind":"cli","id":"mikeschinkel@m4macmini.local","session_id":"1130","harness":"claude_cli"},"payload":{"title":"Add a user-level template directory so overrides are not per-project only","description":"templatecmd resolves a template as \u003cproject_root\u003e/.endless/templates/\u003cname\u003e.local.tmpl, then \u003cname\u003e.tmpl, then the Go embed. That is per-project only: a user who wants the same handoff or guide wording across every project they work on must copy the override into each one, and re-copy it whenever a project is added. Add a user-level layer (e.g. ~/.config/endless/templates/) between the project layer and the embed, so precedence runs project .local -\u003e project committed -\u003e user -\u003e embedded. Surfaced from E-2030, where gating the guide on report_gate raised the question of where a user edits shipped text.","phase":"later","status":"untriaged","type":"todo"}}
